    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "373048\nSTATE OF CALIFORNIA\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS\nDIVISION OF HIGHWAYS\nPUBLIC WORKS BUILDING\nELEVENTH AND STREETS\nSACRAMENTO, CALIFORNIA\nADDRESS ALL COMMUNICATIONS\nТО P. O. BOX 1103\nOctober 11th, 1929.\nIN YOUR REPLY PLEASE\nREFER TO FILE NO.\nMr. Joseph J. Phillips\nDepartment of Public Works,\nCity of San Francisco,\nSan Francisco, California.\nDear Sir:\nYour Letter of October Ist regarding spur track\nrailroad crossings over the Bay Shore Highway received.\nThe State Highway Commission and the Director\nof Public Works have gone on record as opposed to any crossings\nof the Bay Shore Highway at grade; also that the number of cross-\nings by means of grade separations shall be held down to a\nminimum.\nYours very truly,\nBoineer?"
